To run this:

1.  **Save the files:** Save the code above as `ace-editor.js`, `main.js`, and `browserify.js` in the same directory.
2.  **Install Browserify:**  `npm install -g browserify`
3.  **Run Browserify:** Execute the `browserify.js` script from your terminal: `node browserify.js`
4.  **Include the bundle in your HTML:**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Ace Editor Example</title>
  <script src="bundle.js"></script>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/ace/1.4.1/ace.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div id="aceEditor" style="width: 800px; height: 400px;"></div>
  <script src="main.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

This setup creates a `bundle.js` file containing the Ace Editor library and your application code.  The HTML includes the `bundle.js` file and the Ace Editor CSS.  The `main.js` file initializes the editor and sets some initial content.  The `ace-editor.js` file encapsulates the Ace Editor instantiation logic.  The `browserify.js` script uses Browserify to bundle the JavaScript files into a single file, suitable for inclusion in a web page.

